  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: tcp: restrict SO_ATTACH_FILTER to priv users (CVE-2026-53236)\n  * kernel: fuse: re-lock request before replacing page cache folio (CVE-2026-53388)\n  * kernel: net: shaper: rework the VALID marking (again) (CVE-2026-64027)\n  * kernel: net/handshake: hand off the pinned file reference to accept_doit (CVE-2026-63979)\n  * kernel: net/handshake: Drain pending requests at net namespace exit (CVE-2026-63978)\n  * kernel: af_unix: Fix UAF read of tail->len in unix_stream_data_wait() (CVE-2026-64109)\n  * kernel: net/handshake: Take a long-lived file reference at submit (CVE-2026-64523)\n  * kernel: net: gro: fix double aggregation of flush-marked skbs (CVE-2026-68136)\n  * kernel: net/packet: avoid fanout hook re-registration after unregister (CVE-2026-68338)\n  * kernel: scsi: target: core: Fix iSCSI ISID use-after-free in REGISTER AND MOVE (CVE-2026-72083)\n  * kernel: KVM: s390: pci: Reject adapter interrupt forwarding if already enabled (CVE-2026-74515)\n  * kernel: net: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice (CVE-2026-74631)\n  * kernel: usb: usbfs: fix use-after-free of usb_device in usbdev_release() (CVE-2026-80824)\n  * kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n  * kernel: vfio/pci: clear vdev->msi_perm after freeing it on init failure (CVE-2026-89777)\n  * kernel: md/raid5-ppl: fix use-after-free in ppl_do_flush() (CVE-2026-93262)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * x86/microcode: Add platform mask to Intel microcode \"old\" list [AlmaLinux-10] [almalinux-10.2.z] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-212778)\n  * net: NULL pointer deref kernel panic in fib6_walk_continue under heavy VRF churn [almalinux-10.2.z] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-245489)\n  * backport fixes for lockdep issues reported with rt-debug [almalinux-10.2.z] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-259937)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
